---
description: Run code in a Runtime Cloud sandbox instead of on this machine, or move a project's sandbox work to Runtime.
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the `runtime` MCP server when a task needs untrusted or unfamiliar code run,
packages installed, a long job, a clean Linux machine or a web app shared at a
URL. Follow the instructions the server sends when it connects.

- If the Runtime server lists only `runtime_connect`, call it, show the user
  the link and code it returns, and call it again after they approve. Never
  ask for a key.
- Create a sandbox with `runtime_machines_create` (`product` `sandboxes`), run
  commands with `runtime_machines_exec` and check `exitCode` rather than call
  success, and delete every sandbox you started with `runtime_machines_delete`,
  confirming `state` is `deleted`. For one command, `runtime_run` does all
  three. Find any other call with `runtime_search_tools`.
- To move a project from another sandbox provider, read
  https://withruntime.com/llms.txt and the Switch guide it lists for that
  provider, and follow it.
